Vendored upstream copies (verbatim, not rewritten by the alias plugin)
--------------------------------------------------------------------
plan.md decision D2-a requires the replacement `Renderer/Context` to delegate **wholesale** to the
upstream WebGL2 implementation when the device hand-off slot is empty. Because the manifest is static
and the alias plugin rewrites every route to `Source/Renderer/Context.js`, the patch layer carries a
copy of that one file, byte-identical except for its import block (relative specifiers rewritten to the
equivalent bare deep specifiers so it can live outside the upstream `Source` tree) plus a licence /
modification header:

  packages/cesium-webgpu/backend-webgpu/vendor/upstream-webgl2/Context.js
  packages/cesium-webgpu/backend-webgpu/vendor/upstream-webgl2/PROVENANCE.json   (sha256 + rationale)

Regenerate with `node tools/scripts/vendor-upstream-webgl2-context.mjs`; verify with `--check`. The
copy is dormant on the WebGPU path: nothing imports it there, so it never acquires a GL context, never
holds a device and never draws (plan.md D2-a's principle-II argument).

Derived-file header convention
------------------------------
Every file that reimplements or adapts an upstream module MUST keep the original copyright
header and add the note "Modified for WebGPU backend":

    /**
     * @license
     * Copyright 2011-2024 CesiumJS Contributors
     * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
     *
     * Modified for WebGPU backend: module-level replacement of `Source/Renderer/<File>.js` …
     */

Files that are new to this project (everything under backend-webgpu/webgpu/**) MUST carry
`SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0` and state that they are not derived from an upstream file.
tools/scripts/check-license-notice.mjs enforces both rules on every patch-layer file.

Third-party dependencies
------------------------
The license gate reads the `license` field of every installed package and rejects GPL/AGPL,
unknown and absent licenses; the full table is archived as artifacts/license-notice.json.
Notable entries: @cesium/engine (Apache-2.0, pinned 26.3.0), @rollup/plugin-commonjs (MIT, 29.0.3,
build-time only — see docs/gate-g1-conclusion.md F-1), yaml (ISC), rollup and the @rollup/plugin-*
packages (MIT), typescript (Apache-2.0), @webgpu/types (BSD-3-Clause), playwright (Apache-2.0),
rollup-plugin-dts (LGPL-3.0-only, build-time only — never shipped in the deliverable).

